import{_ as t,o,c as i,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 259 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Comparison With Gu Chensha: Differences Between Solitary-Tree and Bestowal Styles","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 259 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Comparison With Gu Chensha: Differences Between Solitary-Tree and Bestowal Styles","no":259,"module":2,"tags":["Tang-Luo","Gu Chensha","Dragon Seal","Solitary-Tree","Bestowal","Myriad-Realms Benchmark"],"related":["29-Symbiosis Degree Evaluation System","30-Five Symbiotic Civilization Typology Overview","01-Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0259_模块2-唐罗-古尘沙对比篇.md","filePath":"en/0259_模块2-唐罗-古尘沙对比篇.md"}'),n={name:"en/0259_模块2-唐罗-古尘沙对比篇.md"};function a(r,e,l,h,u,c){return o(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="entry-259-tang-luo-decomposition-comparison-with-gu-chensha-differences-between-solitary-tree-and-bestowal-styles" tabindex="-1">Entry 259 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Comparison With Gu Chensha: Differences Between Solitary-Tree and Bestowal Styles <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-259-tang-luo-decomposition-comparison-with-gu-chensha-differences-between-solitary-tree-and-bestowal-styles" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 259 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Comparison With Gu Chensha: Differences Between Solitary-Tree and Bestowal Styles&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Tang-Luo System (Entry 9)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-two-people-who-bear-things-on-behalf-of-all-beings" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Two people who &quot;bear things on behalf of all beings&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-two-people-who-bear-things-on-behalf-of-all-beings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Two people who &quot;bear things on behalf of all beings&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the collective ascension axiom opposes &quot;strong ones ascending alone.&quot; Gu Chensha (Dragon Seal) and Tang Luo, on the surface both top strong ones who &quot;bear things on behalf of all beings,&quot; but Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judgment places them in two tiers: Gu Chensha = extreme dependency / solitary-tree type, Tang Luo = high dependency / bestowal style. This entry takes the law-first axiom as core, dissecting the structural roots of these two tiers&#39; difference. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>First compare Gu Chensha system&#39;s energy-level waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Gu Chensha&#39;s waste</strong>: the first in history to cultivate Heavenly Dao Fa, his Sacred Dao is sky-mending and sky-reforming Dao, willing to bear all sentient beings&#39; sins and karma on their behalf; late casually creates cosmoses. His energy is cosmos-creation-tier, but he spends it on &quot;atoning for all beings&quot; — karma could have been cultivated by all beings themselves; once he takes it all, all beings permanently lose the chance to cultivate it themselves</li><li><strong>Tang Luo&#39;s waste</strong>: energy is civilization-reconstruction-tier, spent on &quot;universal benefit within humanity,&quot; the radius one notch smaller than Gu Chensha&#39;s, but still super-large talent super-small use</li></ul><p>The two&#39;s waste forms differ: Gu Chensha is <strong>creation-tier energy used to atone for others</strong>, Tang Luo is <strong>reconstruction-tier energy used for intra-racial allocation</strong>. The former wastes in radius&#39;s infinite expansion (one person carries the whole cosmos), the latter wastes in radius&#39;s over-contraction (carrying only one race).</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Gu Chensha system&#39;s regression</strong>: all beings outsource karma to &quot;history&#39;s first,&quot; their own causal self-discipline ability completely atrophies. Gu Chensha is here, the cosmos is at peace; once Gu Chensha&#39;s Dao dissipates, billions of beings are instantly drowned by the karma they themselves accumulated — this is solitary-tree civilization&#39;s typical collapse</li><li><strong>Tang Luo system&#39;s regression</strong>: bestowal-style dependency, Tang Luo retires, institutional vacuum, old forces restore. Regression speed is slower than Gu Chensha&#39;s, because Tang Luo at least left the skeleton of academies, methods, organizations</li></ul><p>Regression rhythm difference: solitary-tree is <strong>sudden collapse</strong> (one log breaks, the whole house falls), bestowal is <strong>slow regression</strong> (the skeleton remains, but the soul is gone). Tang Luo&#39;s system has one more layer of organizational redundancy than Gu Chensha&#39;s, so it regresses slower — but is still regressing.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Gu Chensha&#39;s predation</strong>: he &quot;is willing to bear everything on behalf of all beings,&quot; on the surface most selfless, actually deprives all beings of the fundamental right to &quot;bear karma themselves, grow on their own.&quot; The greater he is, the more pygmies all beings become. This is &quot;extreme dependency&quot; tier&#39;s predation form — repaying all with virtue, all beings forever owe him, forever cannot be his equal</li><li><strong>Tang Luo&#39;s predation</strong>: he gives all beings favors, making all beings attach. The predation form is &quot;attachment,&quot; not &quot;compensation.&quot; Attachers can at least cultivate on their own, only cultivation direction is set by the benefactor</li></ul><p>By the Gu Chensha / Tang Luo judgment table:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Gu Chensha</th><th>Tang Luo</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Uniqueness dependency</td><td>Extreme</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Civilization form</td><td>Solitary-tree</td><td>Bestowal style</td></tr><tr><td>Predation form</td><td>Compensation (living for you)</td><td>Attachment (living on you)</td></tr><tr><td>All beings&#39; subject</td><td>Those made into dragons</td><td>Recipients</td></tr><tr><td>Collapse speed</td><td>Sudden</td><td>Slow regression</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Solitary-Tree / Bestowal</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis Network Style</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gu Chensha bears sins for all beings</td><td>All beings&#39; causal self-discipline, causal self-discipline axiom written into constitution, cross-plane operations observe first then limitedly interfere</td></tr><tr><td>Tang Luo bestows on all beings</td><td>Myriad Races republican co-building, evolution qualification naturalized</td></tr><tr><td>One person bears / one person gives</td><td>Alaya whole-network sharing, multi-layer supervision, distributed sharing</td></tr><tr><td>Made into dragons / almsgiven</td><td>Co-becoming dragons / co-legislating, everyone is a contracting party</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Alternative&#39;s crux: whether &quot;bearing for you&quot; or &quot;giving you candy,&quot; neither is as good as &quot;building with you.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: respectively replicate Gu Chensha solitary-tree and Tang Luo bestowal-style two civilization models</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: simultaneously let both protagonists&#39; &quot;Dao dissipate,&quot; observe collapse curves</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: Gu Chensha group collapse time &lt;10 years, Tang Luo group collapse time about 50–100 years</li><li><strong>Review conclusion</strong>: bestowal style survives half a century more than solitary-tree, but the illness is the same — both bet civilization on one person</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Gu Chensha system</strong>: setting self-consistency medium-high, combat ceiling extremely high but world-view still self-consistent; retcon-ending risk medium — late power inflates to &quot;casually creating cosmoses,&quot; plot has no more room to level up, can only prop up with &quot;stronger cosmoses&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang Luo system</strong>: setting self-consistency medium-high; retcon-ending risk medium</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency comparison</strong>: Gu Chensha = extreme, Tang Luo = high. The essence of the two-tier gap: Gu Chensha did not even leave an organizational skeleton, Tang Luo at least left the academy and institutional prototype — although the prototype decays, it is better than nothing</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: creation-tier / reconstruction-tier energy both compressed into one person&#39;s undertaking</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: compensation and attachment are predation&#39;s two ultimate forms</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo took half a step further than Gu Chensha — left the organization, but not the institutions</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: solitary-tree / bestowal both cannot cover 99%; networks can</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane governance must be distributed; solitary-tree / bestowal both cannot step across planes</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Gu Chensha and Tang Luo, one is &quot;I live for you,&quot; the other is &quot;I give you life.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer: what all beings want is neither of these, but &quot;we live for ourselves.&quot; Between solitary-tree and bestowal, and networks, the last step is merely: step oneself down from civilization&#39;s center.</p><p>In the final analysis, Tang-Luo · comparison with Gu Chensha described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./29-共生度评估体系.html">29-Symbiosis Degree Evaluation System</a> · <a href="./30-五种共生文明分型总览.html">30-Five Symbiotic Civilization Typology Overview</a> · <a href="./01-锚点共生文明宣言.html">01-Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const m=t(n,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
